@startuml components
title M-CB1: broker components - v0 software root, design only
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Person" as Person
component "Phone app\noperator device key in secure element\nbiometric confirmation" as Phone
component "Operator command\nswarma-operator: account owner / operator\nno harness sessions or shell" as Admin
component "Read-only client\nswarma-observer; no harness sessions" as Observer
database "Protected operator storage\nswarma-operator: v0 Ed25519 private root\noperator records; no agent access" as OperatorStore
component "Caller: Curator composition\ncaller OS account" as Caller
component "swarma-dispatcher\nown service OS account" as Dispatcher
component "curator-run\nactive agent UID + generation\nfirst consumer, slice 0" as Executor
component "Harness\nagent OS account" as Harness
component "swarma-user-manager\nroot, no-argument sudo entry" as Helper
component "Existing service manager\nqualified containment / kill-and-confirm\nrestore start check" as Manager
component "Dedicated broker proxy listener\nv1 service profile; qualified vendor allowlist" as Proxy
component "Approved Codex executable\nbroker service UID, pinned digest\nslice 1" as Codex
database "Helper ledger\nroot-owned, no secrets" as Ledger

package "swarma-credential-broker daemon: one unprivileged service UID" {
  component "Peer authenticator\nkernel effective UID; fixed role\nbroker/1 Unix socket only" as Peer
  component "Principal / UID-generation reader\nactive helper generation or pinned identity" as Identity
  component "Grant verifier + revocations\ntwo separate chains; v0 software root" as Grants
  component "Binding index\nverified admission class\ndispatcher bind / replacement / unbind" as Bindings
  component "Lease service\nclass/freeze gates + checks 1-7; binding/time + 2-7 under state lock\nownership on renew/release/report" as Leases
  component "Account management + auth owner\none internal refresher per rotating account\nslice 1 Codex adapter" as Accounts
  component "Events / audit writer\ntyped metadata only" as Events
  database "Durable store: broker UID\naccounts + secrets, config, grants,\nrevocations, bindings/class evidence, leases,\nR-ALLSTOP journal, time evidence, audit" as Store
}

Caller --> Dispatcher : request execution with caller-composed plan
Dispatcher --> Helper : create / retire account
Helper --> Ledger : publish generations
Dispatcher --> Peer : bind with admission class (encoding unpublished) / unbind; effect.observe; revocation.check; no material
Person --> Phone : inspect exact act; biometric confirmation
Phone --> Admin : SSH over tailnet, pinned key only; forced command; signed act
Person --> Admin : terminal sudo: password; timestamp_timeout=0; no NOPASSWD
Admin --> OperatorStore : admitted act uses account-held authority
Admin --> Peer : admitted owner/operator acts, including R-ALLSTOP; fresh operator connection
Observer --> Peer : status / account.list / grant.list / binding.list; no confirmation
Executor --> Peer : fresh connection; lease methods
Executor --> Harness : env: exec replaces executor; stdin process model unpublished\nexternal-token: start private app-server; retain live client (§8.5, §9.3)
Peer --> Identity : authenticate principal
Identity --> Ledger : direct read at bind / lease / renew
Peer --> Bindings : dispatcher administration / authorized effect.observe
Peer --> Leases : bound trusted-class local agent only; circle membership insufficient (§4.2)
Peer --> Accounts : owner methods
Peer --> Grants : grant / revocation publication; revocation.check
Bindings --> Grants : leaf chain and caller chain separately
Leases --> Bindings : active binding, UID + generation
Leases --> Grants : current authorisation + revocation state
Leases --> Accounts : active, qualified account / channel
Accounts --> Codex : enrol / refresh only after prior writer/outcome resolved
Accounts --> Manager : qualified contained lifecycle; no guardian service
Manager --> Codex : contain / kill / confirm all writer absence
Codex --> Proxy : v1 login / refresh; explicit proxy variables; no direct fallback
Bindings --> Store : receiver intent / result / removal tombstones; binding records
Grants --> Store : signed grants + durable revocations
Leases --> Store : lease metadata; no payload
Accounts --> Store : durable refresh attempt intent before launch; accounts + secrets
Leases --> Events : outcomes / reports
Accounts --> Events : expiry / refresh state metadata
Events --> Store : append-only audit metadata

note bottom of Events
  V0 status-only: operator detection through swarma-observer reads (§11).
  No automatic phone notification; containment/stop never waits for delivery.
  Later owned bounded alert route is unpublished/unqualified (§18.22);
  notification carries no operator act authority and adds no egress route.
end note

note top of Admin
  Verify phone signature bound to one canonical act; no reuse for another.
  Widening: authentication + exact content confirmation;
  refused inside agent sessions. Narrowing: authentication only.
  Operator device key does not replace the Ed25519 software root.
  Binary/wire format, signature domain/canonical bytes and phone-key lifecycle
  unpublished (§18.15); terminal fallback needs no phone.
end note
note right of Peer
  Refuse unavailable peer UID, wrong role or server UID.
  Clients check broker UID before sending; close-on-exec,
  no descriptor inheritance/passing. Role never changes.
  [[../spec/broker.md#41-peer-identity-and-connections Spec §4.1]]
end note
note bottom of Identity
  Missing, ambiguous, retired, malformed or unreadable ledger:
  principal_ledger_mismatch; no home search or fallback.
  Changed pinned identity: refuse until operator re-pins.
  [[../spec/broker.md#42-principals Spec §4.2]]
end note
note bottom of Leases
  Wrong chain/binding/account/profile, source conflict or
  unqualified injection: refuse; executor does not exec.
  Unreadable/stale revocations or fenced restore: refuse;
  revocation.check unavailable; no empty-state substitute.
  Claude recovery: re-enrol + restart; no refresh (slice 0).
  Codex: safe backoff only after prior writer/outcome resolved;
  ambiguous rotation: unavailable or re-enrol after writer absence;
  unavailable owner or missed deadline: refuse (slice 1).
  [[../spec/broker.md#82-checks-in-order Spec §8.2]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#122-protected-binding-and-conflicting-sources Spec §12.2]]
end note
note bottom of Store
  Broker owns persistent state; 0700 directories, 0600 secret files.
  State files atomically replaced; revocation ack follows durability.
  Restore mark and history/start evidence survive outside rollback domain;
  reconcile complete acknowledged history or replace old roots/reissue (§15.4).
  Harness can read/copy a leased token; already copied tokens
  end only at expiry or vendor revocation.
  [[../spec/broker.md#3-components Spec §3]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#124-files Spec §12.4]]
end note
note top of Caller
  Caller process UID is unspecified in spec §3.1.
  Dispatcher socket service from slice 0; no dispatcher sudo entry.
  Only dispatcher invokes privileged launcher; host uses host_start.
  Board runner / session host call dispatcher, not broker.
  Later session runner: agent-side transport / renewal;
  session host: durable session metadata (§3.1).
  SH1/SH2 activation is unspecified in spec §3.1.
end note
note top of Grants
  Keeper identity keys / versioned adapter: later, not v0.
  Source-policy v1/v2 are distinct from broker release phases.
  Enforced networking and service egress: slice 2, helper v1; v0 refuses enforced assurance.
  [[../spec/broker.md#43-trust-root-and-key-classes Spec §4.3]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#16-delivery-order Spec §16]]
end note
note right of Proxy
  Broker network only through proxy (R-SVC-EGRESS).
  Own listener is the sole kernel destination; proxy resolves vendor names.
  Login/refresh/policy-fetch and resolver-bypass rows require qualification.
  Proxy outage: safe transient failure only after writer/outcome resolution.
  User manager §8 owns service rows and scheduled/start re-verification.
  This v1 gate does not disable software-root slice 0 (§15.2).
end note
note bottom of Bindings
  E-rebind: same UID/generation, fresh binding ID; never widens.
  Remove old binding with tombstone, end old leases, then publish new.
  No helper principal; unbind remains dispatcher/operator (§7.3).
end note
note bottom of Accounts
  Muse C7 priority decided: subscription qualification first (§10.2, §18.5).
  PROPOSED (b): one minting owner leases the device-code-OAuth-minted
  provider API key via META_API_KEY / exec --api-key-stdin, never OAuth tokens.
  Fallback (c): key not subscription-billed or revoked by re-mint.
  No OAuth access-token injection; no child linked store. macOS native store
  is Keychain-first, file fallback; replacement inode breaks a linked store.
  Twelve qualification rows open; seven probes need a dedicated test account
  in its own OS user. API-key lane separate; no admitted Muse implementation.
  R-FATE fate table: user manager §7, next to R-FD3;
  stop/crash/replacement and previous-writer fence need platform qualification.
  R-LOCK: state lock never spans synchronous platform-service calls;
  per-record in-flight marker and bounded I/O; stale result cannot deliver (§13.1).
end note
note bottom of Grants
  R-TIME: durable watermark advances only on trusted time;
  expiry checked at max(now, watermark); not_before at min(now, watermark).
  Untrusted time refuses new authority; restore reconciles time evidence.
  Expiry-driven binding removal also needs monotonic lifetime (§15.1).
  R-NETBIND: machine-owned policy, pinned admission and served digest (§5.5).
end note
note bottom of Peer
  R-UNTRUSTED refuses bind/replacement, lease and renewal;
  unavailable class evidence refuses, never inferred from account name.
  R-ALLSTOP journals broker-wide freeze before acknowledgement;
  final delivery after refresh checks it. Direct operator fan-out;
  broker part progresses without dispatcher; containment/stops independent.
  Explicit recovery only after every durable part, including dispatcher, reconciles;
  partial/unknown results keep closed. Delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime.
  Class encoding and node-wide act/records/codes unpublished (§18.16-§18.17).
end note
@enduml
